# Whole Cost hard rules

Single engine: `src/lib/inventory/whole-cost-rules.ts` (wired into price calculator DM cost, Top Vendor Models, sales CSV row margin when a rule matches, `scripts/fill-whole-cost.ts`). Prefer sheet/calculator cost over CSV Profit Amount whenever a rule hits.

## Always (every surface, all historical sales)

1. **Fixed SKU costs** (everyone) — see `FIXED_WHOLE_COST_BY_SKU` (231611→350, …). Match by leading Item # digits (`231618S` → `231618`).
1b. **SKU divisor overrides** — see `SKU_DIVISOR_OVERRIDE` (e.g. `240304` → base ÷ 8.8). Beats design/dept formulas (including GOLD JEWL ÷4).
2. **Design `GOLD JEWL` / `GOLD JEWEL`** + description contains `UV` / `uv` / `ultimate value` (or Class `UV`) → **base ÷ 1.3**
3. **Diamond** (diamond department **or** “diamond” in description) + UV / ultimate value in description → **base ÷ 8.8**  
   - Except the fixed special SKUs above

## Cost base (important)

| Surface | Base for CP divisor rules |
|---|---|
| **Price calculator / onhand / DM cost** | **Tag Price** |
| **Sales dashboard / Top Vendor Models / daily sales report / parse margins** | **Sales Amount** (gross, not Total/net) |

Daily uploads and the sales dashboard (including Jul 1 → Aug 11 seed window and forward) must use Sales Amount × rules, then profit = Net − signed unit cost. Keep return / cancel-leg rules in `top-models-wholesale-margin.ts` (`signedWholesaleUnitCost`, `collapseCancelledSkuLegs`).

Do not invent other gold÷1.3 triggers (e.g. gold department alone without Design GOLD JEWL). Plain GOLD JEWL without UV → ÷ 4 (sheet).

When changing these rules, update `whole-cost-rules.ts`, `public/CP_Divisor_Rules.csv`, and `tests/inventory/pricing-rules.test.ts`.
